From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: add the base texture of every image, view and texel
 buffer texture to the residency set

STEAMAC-G: M3/M4/M5 lose KosmicKrisp devices with
MTL4CommandQueueErrorTimeout right after Steam's UI starts (zink's first
4x MSAA targets, new tiled BGRA8 and linear host-buffer window images) or
after a window resize (gamescope recreating its linear output images).

Metal 4 takes an attachment as resident only when its base texture object
is in a residency set of the command buffer or queue; the heap it was
placed in, the buffer it was made from (host pointer imports) or the view
that is bound do not count. KosmicKrisp only added heaps and buffers, so
Metal API validation reported every render pass ("Attachment texture ...
is not added to any residency set on the command buffer or command
queue", 9033 times in one Steam boot). On an M1 Max it renders anyway.

Image planes add the base texture (parentTexture chain) of their texture
and of the 2D array alias of 3D images when bound, sparse images when
created; block-texel view subresource textures and texel buffer view
textures when created. Each is removed before its release (a residency
set keeps a removed allocation alive until its next commit). Planes that
alias a swapchain image or a drawable add nothing; a plane rebound to a
drawable removes what it added.
